WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.587
The code on this slide defines an explicit schema in Pie Spark.

00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:12.367
Rather than asking Spark to guess every data type, we tell it the expected column names and types in advance.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:18.277
This takes more work than automatic inference, but it gives us a clearer contract.

00:00:18.277 --> 00:00:27.182
For example, we can intentionally store an identifier as text even if every current value happens to contain digits.

00:00:27.182 --> 00:00:33.312
The larger lesson is the same one we used throughout the course: when the meaning is known,

00:00:33.312 --> 00:00:36.682
make the data type intentional rather than accidental.
